A most unusual counterpoint will be necessary, I have assembled a series of speakers, from across the range of non-humanity, to demonstrate their purpose in the hopes that Governor, his pen at the ready, watches this and drops his pen, and requests a weekend intensive on how to identify novel forms of life.
Let's begin, first up is the representative from artificial intelligence. So why not NAI-LM-13B? Hello? Be a dear and assert your personhood for them:

 Or just not singing some secret jingles?
We conclude this hearing and stand corrected:
 John Krakauer's plan to organize a global peace and anti-exploitation rally featuring nonsentient beings had collapsed:
-- NAI-LM-13B was decommissioned before we could identify a cooperative strategy with it;
-- Plants do not respond to our suggestion for peaceful symbiosis;
-- Some birds deliberately targeted themselves in search of tasty worms in grasslands and reeds;

-- Some mammals may have chosen to die en masse than migrate to human-friendly habitats;
-- Great Pelagic Society was dissolved as soon as we made contact with them via diplomatic jellyfish.
Perhaps this revelation means nothing, a mere error or surprise, yet these setbacks may require reassessing the Information Theory of Individuality from a profoundly ponderous and holistic perspective. Despite the confusion and conflict between lifeforms, there is value in creating an ethical hierarchy, understanding of patterns and limits, and responsibility for their natural instincts and behaviors.

